			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Replace polling loops with async notifies and wire native IPC handlers\n\nRefactor extension scanning and sidecar connection logic to replace busy-wait polling with `tokio::sync::Notify` synchronization primitives. Introduce `ExtensionState.ScanReady` and per-sidecar connection notifiers to unblock callers (e.g., `extensions:getInstalled`, `WaitForClientConnection`) immediately upon state transition, eliminating 50ms polling intervals and reducing boot latency.\n\nImplement full handlers for the `nativeHost` lifecycle surface (Exit, Quit, Relaunch, Reload, KillProcess, Install/UninstallShellCommand) and filesystem watching (`file:watch`, `file:unwatch`). These replace previous stub acknowledgments, enabling proper process management and native file system event routing to extensions.\n\nOptimize high-frequency gRPC notification paths (`RegisterCommand`, `ProgressReport`, `DecorationTypeLifecycle`) by migrating from per-call task spawning to a single long-lived mpsc-backed batch flusher. This reduces IPC saturation and task overhead during extension boot by coalescing thousands of rapid updates into single frame-aligned events.\n\nUpdate `Entitlements.plist` to use block-style XML formatting and clarify sandbox exemptions for the non-sandboxed editor environment.",
			"SHA": "41b8029154da51b0556aa59039f99e6a7751c31c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T00:58:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1492,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement dual-layer debug server and SCM diff handling\n\nUpgrade the `WebkitServer` debug utility into a configurable dual-layer diagnostics tool supporting independent activation for the Mountain (Rust) and Cocoon (Node.js) layers. Introduce a unified `DebugServer` environment variable to select mode (mountain, cocoon, both, or off) and distinct ports (default 9933/9934). Add new HTTP endpoints for layer discovery (`/health`, `/layers`), iframe inspection, workbench command invocation, and transparent HTTP proxying to the Cocoon extension host.\n\nImplement the `vscode.diff` and `$scm:openDiff` command handlers in `SCM.rs` to bridge the VS Code Git extension with the editor UI. When triggered, these commands now forward the request to the `sky://editor/diff` endpoint via the Effect system, ensuring the native backend correctly resolves the promise and opens the diff editor as expected.\n\nThese changes restore full debuggability across the full stack and enable native Git workflows by correctly handling the canonical diff command invoked by upstream VS Code extensions.",
			"SHA": "6ae748d57faee496b259c4f513cf2c296f4dc585"
		},
